WEBVTT

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:02.390
Pay attention.

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:04.500
It looks like he's going to 
lay his cards on the table.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:09.090
Yuichi! What the hell have you done?!

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:12.610
I had a plan,

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.490
even before the second game started,

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:19.580
to set traps to smoke out the traitor.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.120
After that one bad-mouth 
in the third period...

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:28.420
"And the same Sawaragi Shiho 
used to date Mikasa Tenji."

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.690
After that came out, Sawaragi and I decided

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:34.680
to work together without the others knowing.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:38.100
Without us knowing? How could...

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.310
There wasn't any way for
 you two to talk it over.

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:42.570
You're right.

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:46.810
That's why we planned it mostly 
without speaking to each other.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.230
I gave Sawaragi instructions 
using the bad-mouth cards.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:55.950
Yes. This is the first trap Yuichi set.

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:56.660
<b>Episode 6: I Really Can't Be Friends with a "Murderer"</b>

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:59.560
Look closely at this footage 
from the fourth period.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:59.580
<b>Episode 6: I Really Can't Be Friends with a "Murderer"</b>

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:01.230
Hmm?

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:03.870
Oh! He took two cards!

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.710
Correct. And after that?

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.130
He's holding a pen.

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:10.280
So what?

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:11.920
Try to remember what happened.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:14.990
What did he say when 
he came out of the room?

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.690
Okay, I left mine blank.

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:25.310
Yes. He said he put in a blank card, 
but he was holding a pen.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:27.100
That does contradict what he said!

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:28.550
You can see in the video

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:33.480
that he was using the bad-mouth cards 
for some other purpose.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.280
Now I see. The cards!

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.880
That's when he handed her one.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:43.290
And then Shiho-chan read it 
when she was in the room.

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:47.000
But how could you trust 
Shiho-chan so easily?

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.750
There was a chance she was the traitor, too.

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:52.370
Obviously, I didn't trust her right away.

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:54.080
I made her pass a test first.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.050
A test?

00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:58.500
The first instructions 
I wrote on the card were,

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:02.840
"Do you remember that old secret 
between just the two of us?"

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:05.390
"Use that to bad-mouth me in this period."

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:09.770
You have to tell me a secret, 
something that the other three don't know.

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:13.800
It was a secret I told Sawaragi 
after she got in the fight with Shibe...

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:14.610
And it was...

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:19.240
"Katagiri Yuichi once didn't 
take a bath for a week."

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:21.410
It was our secret.

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:31.170
Fourth Period Exposés

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:31.170
Who Wrote It

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:31.170
Katagiri Yuichi once didn't 
take a bath for a week.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:31.170
Sawaragi (confirmed)

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:24.790
Sawaragi and I are the only ones 
who could have written it.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:31.170
Shibe Makoto took baths with 
his mother until junior high.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.860
So the big exposés written 
by the traitor in the fourth period

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:31.170
Sawaragi Shiho had plastic surgery.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:28.940
-Shibe 
-Tenji 
-Kokorogi

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.170
Remaining

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:31.170
must not have come from Sawaragi.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.170
-Shibe 
-Tenji 
-Kokorogi

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:35.420
That's when I first trusted 
Sawaragi to be on my side.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:40.260
Next, I wanted to determine 
if Kokorogi was the traitor or not.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.060
Yeah.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.090
Hold on.

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:45.800
In order to find the traitor, 
you were checking us one by one?

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:46.850
That's right.

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:50.240
I found out who the traitor was

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:52.480
through a process of elimination.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:57.610
In the fifth period, I quietly passed 
a bad-mouth card to Kokorogi, too.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.160
It said,

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:00.970
"Sawaragi is on our side,"

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:04.620
"but keep pretending to fight with her 
so we can smoke out the traitor."

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:06.930
"And in the next period,"

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:09.870
"submit a secret about Sawaragi 
that only you know."

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:12.170
That's when she read it!

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:15.540
The card Kokorogi submitted 
in the sixth period said,

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:20.930
"Sawaragi Shiho actually 
usually wears men's boxers."

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:24.980
If there was another big exposé 
that seemed to come from the traitor,

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:26.560
it would clear Kokorogi.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:29.180
And there was.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:32.390
Mikasa Tenji is actually 
lying about his age.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:34.670
Mikasa Tenji is lying about his age

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:36.430
Sixth Period Exposés

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:36.430
Sawaragi Shiho usually wears men's boxers

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:36.430
Kokorogi

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:38.400
* Yuichi and Sawaragi submitted blanks

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:38.400
Who Wrote It

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:36.220
There were only two left 
who could have written that.

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:36.430
Mikasa Tenji is lying about his age

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:38.400
It was either you or Shibe.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:42.610
I used the cards to tell Sawaragi 
how things were going, of course.

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:46.200
I stayed close to Shiho the 
whole time after that period.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:49.520
You didn't have the 
chance to pass her a card!

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.080
Sure I did. Just three minutes.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:55.230
Y-You can't mean...

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:58.820
Right then?!

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:01.700
That was his second trap.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:03.070
Whoa!

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:05.420
The order that people use the room

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:07.760
isn't supposed to make 
a difference in the game.

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:11.630
Okay, I left mine blank. You're next.

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:13.390
But, very nonchalantly...

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:17.770
Sorry Tenji, but could you go first?

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:19.020
Again and again...

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:22.610
Ah, I guess I'll go.

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:25.540
He controlled the order they went in.

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:29.870
In other words, it was all calculated.

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:32.250
The only ones left were you and Shibe,

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.380
but that was easy to decide.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.000
The special chance.

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:37.000
<b><b>Special Chance</b></b>

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:42.010
Since the management knew who
 applied to play Tomodachi Game,

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:45.870
it would have been too risky 
for the traitor to volunteer.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:50.250
So that left only you, Tenji.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:55.540
That means the fighting between 
Shiho-chan and Kokorogi-san was all an act?

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:59.000
Well, I might have taken it 
a little seriously.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.030
Me, too. Sorry.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:03.110
So that strategy was...

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:07.300
Listen. From here on, all of us 
except the person in the lead,

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:09.490
should bad-mouth <i>ourselves</i>.

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:11.620
That was part of your plan, too?

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:15.710
Yeah. I knew that strategy 
had holes in it from the start.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:17.830
Do you remember what I said?

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:21.630
Our debt shouldn't increase 
from here on out.

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:26.330
Mikasa Tenji

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:24.460
That gave me the final confirmation—

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:28.890
whether you betrayed us for money, 
or for something else.

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:32.950
You didn't back off then,

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:34.980
so it looked like it was something else.

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:40.520
W-Why didn't you reveal that 
I was the traitor right away?

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:43.070
We still had the second half to play.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:46.160
If you knew you got caught, 
you might have gone wild

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:49.950
<b>Clean that up yourself</b>

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:49.620
and written a bunch of other things. 
I wanted to avoid that.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:52.470
So I kept you barely in check...

00:05:53.030 --> 00:05:55.700
All right. Why don't you 
go write first, then.

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:57.040
Huh?!

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:58.870
Mikasa Tenji

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:00.330
and in the last period, 
when you went in the room,

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:03.300
I told everyone else to put in blank cards.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:07.760
But that doesn't make sense. It doesn't!

00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:11.100
You said you used a process 
of elimination to smoke me out.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:15.390
But everyone can write 
as many cards as they want.

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:15.390
<b>- You can write as many things as you want about each person</b>

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:19.020
Your process of elimination wouldn't work!

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:22.480
Yes, thus his third and final trap.

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:25.110
His boldest and most cunning one yet.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:28.070
Smart as always, Tenji. 
That's exactly right.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:34.080
"Katagiri Yuichi once didn't
 take a bath for a week."

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:30.610
Since anyone could write 
as many cards as they wanted,

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:34.080
"Sawaragi Shiho had plastic surgery."

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:34.080
Both were written by Sawaragi.

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:34.080
even the first time with Sawaragi, 
I couldn't clear her with that alone.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.930
And so, when I tested them,

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:38.290
I made them give me proof 
of their friendship.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:40.190
Proof of their friendship?

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:43.920
Didn't you notice? 
Isn't there something different?

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:50.970
T-Their...

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:54.680
Their name tags are missing!

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:56.850
Bingo.

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:58.100
People do it all the time,

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:02.100
trading valuables with someone 
else as proof of friendship.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:02.100
Shibe Makoto

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:02.100
Sawaragi Shiho

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:02.100
Kokorogi Yutori

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:07.860
I told them I'd trust them if they let me 
hold on to their precious name tags.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:10.990
They weren't traitors, so they 
immediately handed them over.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:12.760
T-That's...

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:16.760
Would you have expected Kokorogi to
 suddenly believe Sawaragi was on her side?

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:18.700
I gave her a note.

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:23.330
<b>Sawaragi Shiho</b>

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:23.330
It said, "I have Sawaragi's name tag. 
She won't betray us."

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:26.980
Kokorogi Yutori

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:29.050
Then Kokorogi gave me her name tag, 
and finally Shibe did, too.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:29.050
Shibe Makoto

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:32.360
Your debt doesn't double if you
 just hand the tag to someone.

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:34.440
I'm impressed he figured that out!

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:35.930
It seems he tested it.

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:40.180
At one point before the fourth period, 
his name tag was missing.

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:42.790
He probably secretly handed it to Sawaragi,

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:44.770
most likely while Shibe and 
Mikasa were fighting.

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:46.190
You're right.

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:50.570
And then he got his name tag back 
when he handed her the card.

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:54.660
There's an eye-tracking camera built 
into the screen on the tag,

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:57.280
so it can tell if they looked 
at the back or not.

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:00.380
After testing it, 
he wrote a note to Sawaragi

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:02.700
telling her to hand him her name tag.

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:05.730
See? Right here, she isn't wearing hers.

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:09.050
Heh. Bold and cunning, indeed.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:13.180
In order to keep them from betraying him 
and writing multiple cards,

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:15.800
Sawaragi Shiho

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:15.800
Kokorogi Yutori

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:15.800
Shibe Makoto

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:15.800
he kept their name tags hostage.

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:19.810
It's as if he was telling them, "If you 
hand over your tag, I'll trust you."

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:22.180
"If not, I won't."

00:08:22.570 --> 00:08:26.310
Sawaragi must have known she 
absolutely couldn't refuse.

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:29.440
Sawaragi Shiho

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:30.730
And then like a chain reaction, 
they all had to hand them over.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:31.440
Kokorogi Yutori

00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:33.450
They knew that if they didn't, 
they'd be isolated.

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:33.400
Shibe Makoto

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:38.080
Only a very devious mind can prey 
on the weakness of others like that.

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:43.210
He knows all about human weakness, 
and about the power and terror of money.

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:46.330
His thought process is similar to the way

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:49.340
that religious cults and
 pyramid schemes operate.

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:53.490
But at the end, everyone was able to 
finish the game with a smile on their face,

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:52.780
<i>Here, I'll return these. I didn't 
look at the backs, of course.</i>

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:53.490
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:55.210
so didn't it all turn out okay?

00:08:55.210 --> 00:08:56.360
It's the opposite.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:09:00.750
The fact that they're still smiling 
after handing over their name tags,

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:04.040
which are the lifeblood of this game, 
is absolutely chilling.

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:09.990
This expert liar, who tricked the others 
and still left them smiling...

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:13.500
Who is this man, really?

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:16.960
Yuichi...

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:19.280
Tell me one last thing.

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:22.620
Why... Why me?

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:27.500
<b>lololol</b>

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:27.500
<b>now that you mention it...</b>

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:27.500
<b>in your face lol</b>

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:27.500
<b>Tenji-kun cyute</b>

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:27.500
<b>serves you right</b>

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:27.500
<b>sucks for you</b>

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:27.500
<b>brilliant deduction</b>

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:27.500
<b>I knew it from the start lol</b>

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:27.500
<b>it's over \(^o^)/</b>

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:27.500
You started with the friends you trusted 
and made them allies one by one.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:32.170
That means you always thought 
I was the most suspicious, right?

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:36.170
Did I... Did I make a mistake somewhere?

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:44.270
<b>they hate you now</b>

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:44.270
<b>absolutely lol</b>

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:44.270
<b>pathetic lmao</b>

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:44.270
<b>lol duh</b>

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:44.270
<b>you lost</b>

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:44.270
<b>that's it!</b>

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:44.270
<b>lolololol</b>

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:44.270
<b>i'm crying lmaooo</b>

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:44.270
<b>hilariously obvious lol</b>

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:44.270
<b>duh lmao</b>

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:44.270
<b>lmaoooo</b>

00:09:37.650 --> 00:09:40.630
Well, not exactly a mistake.

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:44.270
I think I know you guys pretty well.

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:45.710
So...

00:09:46.450 --> 00:09:50.650
It was suspicious when you weren't 
acting like yourself during the game.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:52.940
I wasn't... like myself?

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:56.720
The Tenji I know is smart and calm.

00:09:56.720 --> 00:10:00.030
If we start arguing, 
you step in to break it up.

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:04.040
But at the start of the game, 
you picked a fight with Shibe.

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:07.790
You said it was Shibe 
who wrote that bad-mouth.

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:09.920
Do you seriously think that would happen?

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:14.300
<b>- The game is played in periods 
- Each period, you bad-mouth someone 
- Write it down on the bad-mouth card in the private room 
- Once you enter the private room, you can't leave for three minutes 
- You can write as many things as you want about each person 
- You may submit a blank bad-mouth card 
- You may lie (if the lie is revealed, you'll be forced one space in front of the lead player) 
- The number of spaces you move is determined by the god survey</b>

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:14.300
Bad-Mouth Sugoroku is about
 leaking your friends' secrets.

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:18.200
But it'd be impossible for 
Shibe to bad-mouth us.

00:10:19.270 --> 00:10:20.210
You can't mean...

00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:24.470
Yup. None of us have told
 Shibe any secrets.

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:25.390
Huh!?

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:25.390
<b>Boom!</b>

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:25.390
<b>No way...</b>

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:28.020
Don't tell the others. Especially Shibe.

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:32.010
That's what I said when I told you 
my secret. Right, Sawaragi?

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:33.960
Yeah, it is.

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:38.450
And Kokorogi, you really don't want 
Shibe to know your secrets, right?

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:39.400
Yeah.

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:40.450
<b>Boom!</b>

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:44.780
I mean, Shibe has such a big mouth.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:48.160
Shibe's an awkward idiot.

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:51.040
Even that bad-mouth in the fourth period...

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:55.170
Shibe Makoto took baths with
 his mother until junior high.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:55.050
<b>how cute lol</b>

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:59.510
He probably wrote it himself 
in order to protect Sawaragi.

